# .semgrepignore — Triaged Semgrep suppressions for HRMS
# Each entry below has been reviewed and suppressed with documented justification.
# DO NOT add entries without a comment explaining the rationale.
# Last reviewed: 2026-07-25

# ── Generated / migration files ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# EF Core migrations are auto-generated. Raw SQL strings in Up()/Down() are
# parameterised via EF infrastructure; they are not user-controlled injection risks.
HRMS.Infrastructure/Migrations/

# ── Test files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files intentionally use hard-coded passwords, dummy secrets, and mock data.
# Semgrep secret rules produce many false positives here. Tests run in a sandboxed
# in-memory DB with no real credentials.
HRMS.Tests/

# ── wwwroot vendor bundles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Third-party minified JS/CSS (Bootstrap, etc.) — not our code, already vetted via
# dependency scanning (Dependabot). Semgrep's JS rules create false positives here.
HRMS.API/wwwroot/assets/vendor/

# ── appsettings.Development.json ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev-only config with placeholder values (empty strings, localhost, dev Swagger creds).
# None of these values are used in production. Production config is supplied via
# env vars only (enforced by EnvironmentValidator at startup).
HRMS.API/appsettings.Development.json
